        "id": 3522082,
        "postDate": "2026-09-08T04:03:10.897Z",
        "rawMarkdown": "I’m seeing pretty much the same behavior.\n\nMy motion linker changes give around +0.012 on 5-fold CV on average, with no fold getting worse, but the LB gain is exactly +0.001. I also compared the public 0.946 LB notebook with my older private 0.942 LB notebook under the same 5-fold CV setup, and surprisingly the public one was about 0.015 worse locally. Given that some people have already pointed out possible test-set overfitting in public notebooks, I’m starting to suspect there may also be a fairly large distribution shift between train, public test, and hidden test...?\n\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/competitions/biohub-cell-tracking-during-development/discussion/739278",
        "content": "<p>I’m seeing pretty much the same behavior.</p>\n<p>My motion linker changes give around +0.012 on 5-fold CV on average, with no fold getting worse, but the LB gain is exactly +0.001. I also compared the public 0.946 LB notebook with my older private 0.942 LB notebook under the same 5-fold CV setup, and surprisingly the public one was about 0.015 worse locally. Given that some people have already pointed out possible test-set overfitting in public notebooks, I’m starting to suspect there may also be a fairly large distribution shift between train, public test, and hidden test…?</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/biohub-cell-tracking-during-development/discussion/739278\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/biohub-cell-tracking-during-development/discussion/739278</a></p>",
