            "id": 3522206,
            "postDate": "2026-09-08T12:03:12.330Z",
            "rawMarkdown": "ask chatgpt \"distribution shift between train, public test, and hidden test…\" on how to probe or verify.\nYou definitely can do some online testing/training and send the results back by \"smart encoding your submission\"\n\nalso download more external data or augmentation etc to test locally.\nwhen you evaluate your model on local dataset, don't just look at the numbers. visualise the results and more importantly, explain why (especially statistically). is the error common or will be common? \n",
            "content": "<p>ask chatgpt \"distribution shift between train, public test, and hidden test…\" on how to probe or verify.\nYou definitely can do some online testing/training and send the results back by \"smart encoding your submission\"</p>\n<p>also download more external data or augmentation etc to test locally.\nwhen you evaluate your model on local dataset, don't just look at the numbers. visualise the results and more importantly, explain why (especially statistically). is the error common or will be common? </p>",
