                "id": 3522221,
                "postDate": "2026-09-08T12:50:02.010Z",
                "rawMarkdown": "Root cause not necessarily means why it happens. It can also means will it reliably happen. Eg you can make some smart error correction to repair local track. But will this error actually happens in hidden test ( not why it happens).\n\n\nAs a concept example, you find your gain in local lb is due to repair of gap = 5 missing frames. Then you find that of all broken tracks, 80% is gap1, 18% is gap2 … less than one percent is gap5",
                "content": "<p>Root cause not necessarily means why it happens. It can also means will it reliably happen. Eg you can make some smart error correction to repair local track. But will this error actually happens in hidden test ( not why it happens).</p>\n<p>As a concept example, you find your gain in local lb is due to repair of gap = 5 missing frames. Then you find that of all broken tracks, 80% is gap1, 18% is gap2 … less than one percent is gap5</p>",
