      "rawMarkdown": "Any implementation of a \"smarter\" motion linker—anything beyond a basic algorithm—results in an increase of exactly 0.001.\n\nThe CV may vary by about 0.01–0.03, but the model's performance simply neither worsens nor improves on the LB, which seems strange. \n\nHas anyone encountered this?",
